# The JupyterLab extension's bundle is COMMITTED build output (see
# labextension/README.md), so that building the wheel never needs Node. Pin its
# newlines to LF on every platform: without this, a Windows checkout rewrites
# the emitted JavaScript and the bytes served to the browser are no longer the
# bytes `npm run build` produced and guarded.
#
# Scoped to the extensions the bundle actually ships (.js, .json) rather than
# `**` over the whole directory: a blanket rule would just as happily rewrite
# the newlines of a future binary asset emitted here -- a font, an image, a
# sourcemap -- which is corruption, not normalization. Add an extension here
# only once something under this directory actually ships it.
src/cash/labextension/**/*.js text eol=lf
src/cash/labextension/**/*.json text eol=lf
